G,E,A are collinear [07]
GE = GA [08]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. AB ⟂ BC [00] & AB ∥ CD [01] & BC ∥ AD [02] ⇒  ∠DCB = ∠DAB [09]
002. ∠DCB = ∠DAB [09] ⇒  B,D,C,A are concyclic [10]
003. B,D,C,A are concyclic [10] ⇒  ∠BDA = ∠BCA [11]
004. F,E,D are collinear [05] & FE = FD [06] ⇒  F is midpoint of ED [12]
005. G,E,A are collinear [07] & GE = GA [08] ⇒  G is midpoint of EA [13]
006. F is midpoint of ED [12] & G is midpoint of EA [13] ⇒  FG ∥ DA [14]
007. D,F,E are collinear [05] & D,B,E are collinear [03] & G,E,A are collinear [07] & C,A,E are collinear [04] & ∠BDA = ∠BCA [11] & FG ∥ AD [14] & AD ∥ BC [02] ⇒  ∠FBC = ∠FGC [15]
008. ∠FBC = ∠FGC [15] ⇒  G,C,B,F are concyclic [16]
009. G,E,A are collinear [07] & C,A,E are collinear [04] & FG ∥ AD [14] & AD ∥ BC [02] ⇒  ∠GCB = ∠CGF [17]
010. G,C,B,F are concyclic [16] & ∠GCB = ∠CGF [17] ⇒  GB = CF
